                <pb facs="0478" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg398"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Judge of superior court of Alameda
                            County to the governor of
                        California</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Oakland, Cal.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic">December 21,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of the communication of Mr.
                    Foley of December 12 relative to violations of the consular convention between
                    the Governments of the United States of America and France, and in respect
                    thereto would say that if any such violations are called to my attention I will
                    most willingly do everything in my power to insure the proper enforcement of the
                    provisions of said convention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry A. Melvin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Judge of the Superior Court.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
